    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 272 tests pass, including the new `Cp08Tests`. \n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did to make owners default their registration date to today and expose it in the response:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** (entity): added a persistent `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`, column `registration_date`) with getter/setter.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`**: when a new owner has no registration date, set it to `LocalDate.now()`.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added a read-only `registrationDate` field (`format: date`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and Jackson serializes it as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. It maps automatically via MapStruct by name.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`): added the `registration_date DATE` column, and updated the positional seed `INSERT`s (hsqldb/mysql) to include a value so context startup still succeeds. (h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists, so they were unaffected.)\n\nThe `registrationDate` is returned in the owner response in ISO format, defaulting to today when not supplied.",
